{"name":"Distant Homeworld","hex":"#acdcee","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"distant","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Far off (physically, logically or mentally).","Emotionally unresponsive or unwilling to express genuine feelings."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["This term needs a definition. Please help out and add a definition, then remove the text {{rfdef}}."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/distant"},{"term":"homeworld","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The world on which someone or something originated; a home planet or moon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/homeworld"}],"entries":[{"title":"Homeworld","blocks":[{"text":"Homeworld is a real-time strategy video game developed by Relic Entertainment and published by Sierra Studios on September 28, 1999, for Windows. Set in space, the science fiction game follows the Kushan exiles of the planet Kharak after their home planet is destroyed by the Taiidan Empire in retaliation for developing hyperspace jump technology. The survivors journey with their spacecraft-constructing mothership to reclaim their ancient homeworld of Hiigara from the Taiidan, encountering a variety of pirates, mercenaries, traders, and rebels along the way. In each of the game's levels, the player gathers resources, builds a fleet, and uses it to destroy enemy ships and accomplish mission objectives. The player's fleet carries over between levels and can travel in a fully three-dimensional space within each level rather than being limited to a two-dimensional plane."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4b/Homeworld_%28video_game%29_box_art.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homeworld"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/91/Homeworld_gameplay.jpg/330px-Homeworld_gameplay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/91/Homeworld_gameplay.jpg/330px-Homeworld_gameplay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An in-game screenshot from the original version of the game depicting a battle near the mothership. The mothership is being attacked by beam and missile weapons, and is on fire. The game's user interface is hidden, as is usual during gameplay unless the player has pressed an interface option key.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHomeworld_gameplay.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a8/Homeworld_%28video_game%29_cutscene_screenshot.jpg/330px-Homeworld_%28video_game%29_cutscene_screenshot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a8/Homeworld_%28video_game%29_cutscene_screenshot.jpg/330px-Homeworld_%28video_game%29_cutscene_screenshot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The final hand-drawn cutscene of Homeworld, showing Karan S'jet as the last person from the fleet to set foot on Hiigara","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHomeworld_(video_game)_cutscene_screenshot.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Interaction-Magazine-1999-Spring.jpg/500px-Interaction-Magazine-1999-Spring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Interaction-Magazine-1999-Spring.jpg/1280px-Interaction-Magazine-1999-Spring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Interaction-Magazine-1999-Spring.jpg/500px-Interaction-Magazine-1999-Spring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Homeworld on the cover of Interaction, the magazine of publisher Sierra Studios","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AInteraction-Magazine-1999-Spring.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/87/Homeworld_Remastered_gameplay.png/330px-Homeworld_Remastered_gameplay.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/87/Homeworld_Remastered_gameplay.png/330px-Homeworld_Remastered_gameplay.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An in-game screenshot from the remastered version of the game depicting a battle near the mothership. The mothership is being attacked by beam and missile weapons.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHomeworld_Remastered_gameplay.png"}],"sounds":{"distant":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/38/En-us-distant.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/38/En-us-distant.ogg/En-us-distant.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"The blue of the sky","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/The_blue_of_the_sky.jpg/500px-The_blue_of_the_sky.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_blue_of_the_sky.jpg","share":0.173125},{"title":"Blue Mountains National Park (AU), Three Sisters -- 2019 -- 1987-9","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Blue_Mountains_National_Park_%28AU%29%2C_Three_Sisters_--_2019_--_1987-9.jpg/500px-Blue_Mountains_National_Park_%28AU%29%2C_Three_Sisters_--_2019_--_1987-9.jpg","ratio":0.9647875948958166,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blue_Mountains_National_Park_(AU),_Three_Sisters_--_2019_--_1987-9.jpg","share":0.051875},{"title":"Hazy blue hour in Grand Canyon","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Hazy_blue_hour_in_Grand_Canyo